Package: afake-su
Architecture: aarch64
Depends: bash
Installed-Size: 3420
Section: utils
Priority: optional
Maintainer: @httpspycharmhelpers
Version: 1.2
Homepage: https://github.com/httpspycharmhelpers/aFakeSU
Description: A fake su implementation based on proot
 fakesu is a self-contained proot-based su: it statically embeds proot and
 only needs the system liblog/libdl, so no proot or root are required.
 The rish/rishq bridge harvests the device's real uid/group tables through
 Shizuku; when Shizuku is absent fakesu still runs, it just falls back to
 its built-in defaults. Requires the plain Termux app and aarch64.
 .
 This package takes over $PREFIX/bin/su (owned by termux-tools) and
 $PREFIX/bin/sudo (owned by sudo, when installed) with dpkg-divert, so the
 originals are renamed aside and restored on removal. Nothing is
 uninstalled to make room for it.
